reagent-name-rmcvirusfood = Virus Food
reagent-desc-rmcvirusfood = A mixture of water, milk, and oxygen. Virus cells can use this mixture to reproduce.

reagent-name-rmcammonia = Ammonia
reagent-desc-rmcammonia = A caustic substance commonly used in fertilizers or household cleaners.

reagent-name-rmcnicotine = Nicotine
reagent-desc-rmcnicotine = A legal, highly addictive stimulant extracted from the tobacco plant. One of the most commonly abused drugs.

reagent-name-rmcthermite = Thermite
reagent-desc-rmcthermite = A pyrotechnic composition of powdered iron oxides that is an extremely volatile explosive. Used in hand grenades, incendiary bombs, welding, and ore processing.

reagent-name-rmcspacecleaner = Space Cleaner
reagent-desc-rmcspacecleaner = A synthetic cleaner that vaporizes quickly and isn't slippery like water. Used for cleaning in space and low gravity environments. Very effective at sterilizing surfaces.

reagent-name-rmccryptobiolin = Cryptobiolin
reagent-desc-rmccryptobiolin = A component used in making spaceacillin.

reagent-name-rmcimpedrezene = Impedrezene
reagent-desc-rmcimpedrezene = A narcotic that impedes one's neural abilities by slowing down the higher brain cell functions. Can cause serious brain damage.

reagent-name-rmcfluorosurfactant = Fluorosurfactant
reagent-desc-rmcfluorosurfactant = A perfluorinated sulfonic acid that forms a foam when mixed with water.

reagent-name-rmcfoamingagent = Foaming Agent
reagent-desc-rmcfoamingagent = An agent that yields metallic foam when mixed with light metal and a strong acid.

reagent-name-rmcstabilizedmetallicfoam = Stabilized Metallic Foam
reagent-desc-rmcstabilizedmetallicfoam = Stabilized metallic foam that solidifies when exposed to an open flame.

reagent-name-rmcdiethylamine = Diethylamine
reagent-desc-rmcdiethylamine = Used as a potent fertilizer and as an alternative to ammonia. Also used in the preparation of rubber processing chemicals, agricultural chemicals, and pharmaceuticals.

reagent-name-rmcglycerol = Glycerol
reagent-desc-rmcglycerol = A simple polyol compound, sweet tasting and of low toxicity. Used in medicines and beverages, and in the production of plastic, nitroglycerin, and other explosives.

reagent-name-rmchexamine = Hexamine
reagent-desc-rmchexamine = A crystalline compound with many uses, from food additives to plastics, treating urinary tract infections, smokeless heating elements in military rations, and the creation of several explosives.

reagent-name-rmcoxidizingagent = Oxidizing Agent
reagent-desc-rmcoxidizingagent = A synthesized, highly refined oxidizing agent that is most likely extremely unhealthy for human consumption.

reagent-name-rmcforensicspray = Forensic Spray
reagent-desc-rmcforensicspray = A dye-containing spray that binds to the skin oils left behind by fingerprints.

reagent-name-rmcsleen = Sleen
reagent-desc-rmcsleen = An illicit mixture of name brand lime soda and oxycodone, known for its distinct red hue and narcotic culture.

reagent-name-rmccornoil = Corn Oil
reagent-desc-rmccornoil = An oil derived from various types of corn.

reagent-name-rmcplasticide = Plasticide
reagent-desc-rmcplasticide = Liquid plastic. Not safe to eat.
